url: "https://www.skakarh.com"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - medical-imaging
  - diabetic-retinopathy
  - selective-prediction
  - uncertainty-quantification
  - calibration
  - deep-learning
  - pytorch
abstract: >-
  Benchmark and selective-prediction analysis of deterministic, Bayesian,
  and conformal uncertainty methods applied to retinal disease screening
  (APTOS 2019, with external validation on Messidor-2 and IDRiD). The
  central question is when a deep model should abstain and route a case
  to a clinician, and how much that improves the safety / coverage
  trade-off relative to a deterministic baseline.
